WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:00.980
Welcome back.

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.495
By the end of this lesson, you will be
prepared with the workflow that will

00:00:04.495 --> 00:00:06.649
make it easy for
you to optimize your images so

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:10.357
that they take up as little bandwidth
as possible while still looking great.

00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:12.826
You'll be thinking about
image quality and size.

00:00:12.826 --> 00:00:15.658
And with images on the web,
it all comes down to size, but

00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:17.910
what does that actually mean?

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.570
Here's a question for you.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.260
Can you spot the differences
between these three images?

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.120
To be honest,
I can't tell the difference with my eye.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.830
These three look the same to me.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.330
For this quiz, check out
the site in the instructor notes.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.030
Then use DevTools to work out
the difference between the three images.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.040
Are the differences caused
by compression level,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.760
display resolution, the natural
resolution, or the file type?

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:43.630
Check all that apply.

